Maybe it's more clear with code:

```C#
public static Task MyAsyncApi()
{
    Activity? activity = new Activity("MyAsyncApi").Start();

    DoSomeSyncStuff();

    return Task.Run(Impl);

    void Impl()
    {
        DoBlockingIO();
        activity?.Stop();
    }
}


Task task = MyAsyncApi();
Console.WriteLine(Activity.Current.OperationName); // prints MyAsyncApi

await task;
Console.WriteLine(Activity.Current.OperationName); // still prints MyAsyncApi :(((
```

The only way to ensure that `Activity.Current` will not be set to `MyAsyncApi` on the parent context forever is to reset `Activity.Current` after starting the `MyAsyncApi` Activity.
